# Architecture projects

Projects are data, not HTML. One JSON file per project generates both language versions.

## Files

- Data: `src/_data/projects/[slug].json` (kebab-case slug = file name). URLs: `/projekty/[slug]/` and `/en/projects/[slug]/`.
- Images: `src/images/[slug]/` for hand-added projects (paths start with `/images/[slug]/`); images uploaded in the CMS land flat in `src/images/` as WebP.
- CMS: `src/admin/config.yml` mirrors these fields; change both together.
- Shape: `{ "pl": {...}, "en": {...} }`, both with `title`, `order`, `category`, `location`, `year`, `summary`, `description` (paragraphs separated by a blank line), `credits`, `images: [{ src, alt, slideshow }]`. `src` is a path, or `{ src, x, y }` when the crop point is not the center (`x` and `y` are 0–100). Missing `en` fields fall back to `pl`. `slideshow: true` puts that frame on the homepage show.

## Rendering

- `src/project.njk` renders project pages; `src/index.njk` renders the homepage slideshow and portfolio cards from `projectList` (sorted by `order`).
- First image = card and project hero. The homepage show uses images flagged `slideshow`; if a project has none, it uses the first image. Remaining images: odd count starts with one full-width image, then pairs; even count is pairs only.
- Images are optimized at build time by `@11ty/eleventy-img`; the lightbox (`src/assets/js/lightbox.js`) uses `currentSrc`.
- Do not hand-write project HTML or edit `sitemap.xml`; both are generated.

## Check

`npm run build && npm test` must pass after any change.
